\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Localization and end-to-end accuracy (\%) on 188 verified cases, five folds with every trajectory in one fold. Training on the verifier's labels lifts both architectures on both metrics; the paired test separates neither trained variant from the other. $t$ is the step index at which the need arises; \emph  {net} counts the cases the scorer gets right and the row's condition gets wrong, minus the reverse, with the two-sided McNemar $p$. Prompted full history and the screen index read in their own single call; both per-screen scorer rows and the trained full-history reader use read with history.}}{5}{table.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{2}{5}{Localization and end-to-end accuracy (\%) on 188 verified cases, five folds with every trajectory in one fold. Training on the verifier's labels lifts both architectures on both metrics; the paired test separates neither trained variant from the other. $t$ is the step index at which the need arises; \emph {net} counts the cases the scorer gets right and the row's condition gets wrong, minus the reverse, with the two-sided McNemar $p$. Prompted full history and the screen index read in their own single call; both per-screen scorer rows and the trained full-history reader use read with history}{table.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) Localization by gap. The trained variants are level everywhere except at gaps of 8--12 screens, where the per-screen scorer leads by 21.8 points; at 13 or more both fall below prompted full history. (b) What the free labels buy: the same labels lift both architectures, the scorer twice as much. Numbers are in Tables~\ref {tab:main} and~\ref {tab:gap}.}}{5}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{2}{5}{(a) Localization by gap. The trained variants are level everywhere except at gaps of 8--12 screens, where the per-screen scorer leads by 21.8 points; at 13 or more both fall below prompted full history. (b) What the free labels buy: the same labels lift both architectures, the scorer twice as much. Numbers are in Tables~\ref {tab:main} and~\ref {tab:gap}}{figure.caption.15}{}}
